r " [:a {:href "/athletes/50810"} "Igor Grivennikov"] " led American " [:a {:href ""} "John Kinsella"] " by half a bodylength. On the second leg, " [:a {:href "/athletes/51597"} "Fred Tyler"] " gave the Americans a bodylength lead over West Germany at 400 metres, the Soviets dropping back. But " [:a {:href "/athletes/51355"} "Steve Genter"] " then put the race away with a 1:52.78 split to give Spitz a big lead for the anchor. Spitz came home in a somewhat pedestrian 1:54.24 but it was good enough for the gold medal, a world record 7:35.78, and nearly a six-second margin over the West Germans. The USSR held on to win the bronze medal."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "United States"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "7:46.42 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "7:35.78 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:class "bib"} "564"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/51446"} "John Kinsella"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:class "bib"} "573"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/51597"} "Fred Tyler"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:class "bib"} "558"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/51355"} "Steve Genter"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:class "bib"} "571"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/51572"} "Mark Spitz"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {